        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="which-problem" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Dairy-Free vs Lactose-Free: Which Problem Do You Have?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Two very different conditions send people looking for a non-dairy protein powder, and they call for different products. Lactose intolerance is a digestive problem: your gut makes too little lactase, the enzyme that breaks down milk sugar, so undigested lactose ferments in the colon and causes bloating, gas and loose stools. It is uncomfortable, it depends on the dose, and it is extremely common. A widely cited 2017 analysis in The Lancet Gastroenterology and Hepatology estimated that around two-thirds of the world's population has reduced ability to digest lactose.
          </p>

          <p>
            A milk allergy is an immune reaction to the proteins in milk, mainly casein and the whey proteins. The amount of lactose is irrelevant, because the immune system is reacting to the protein itself. Reactions range from hives and stomach pain to anaphylaxis, and they can be triggered by small amounts. Whey protein, whey isolate, hydrolyzed whey, casein and milk protein isolate are all milk protein, however heavily filtered they are, so none of them is safe for someone with a milk allergy.
          </p>

          <p>
            That gives you a simple rule. If you have a diagnosed milk allergy, or you avoid dairy for vegan or ethical reasons, you need a truly dairy-free powder: plant protein, egg white or beef protein isolate. If lactose is your only problem, a well-filtered whey isolate is usually fine and often the easier option, as our guide to <a href="/whey-vs-whey-isolate/">whey vs whey isolate</a> explains. If you are not sure which you have, an allergist or your doctor can tell you, and that answer is worth more than any product review.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
