                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Your situation</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">What to avoid</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">What works</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Milk allergy</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">All milk protein, including whey isolate and casein</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Plant, egg white or beef isolate powders</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Lactose intolerance</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Whey concentrate, milk-based blends</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Whey isolate, or any dairy-free powder</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Vegan or plant-based</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">All animal products</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Plant proteins only</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Egg allergy plus dairy-free</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Egg white and milk powders</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Plant or beef isolate powders</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            People with both a milk allergy and an egg allergy, which often travel together in childhood, should also skip egg white powder. Anyone managing a diagnosed food allergy should treat this guide as a starting point and confirm every product's allergen statement, and ideally their choice, with an allergist or registered dietitian.
          </p>
