          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Start with the question that decides everything: are you avoiding milk protein or just lactose? With a milk allergy or a vegan diet, choose a powder with no milk ingredients at all. Garden of Life Sport or Vega Sport for a fully dosed, certified plant protein, Naked Pea for a single-ingredient base, or egg white and beef isolate if you eat animal foods but not dairy.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If lactose is the only problem, a lactose-free whey isolate such as Isopure Zero Carb is often the simplest and cheapest route to a complete protein. Either way, read the allergen statement on the exact flavor you buy, and let an allergist or registered dietitian have the final word if your reaction to dairy is more than mild discomfort.
